🎯 Common Interview Questions & Short Answers
1️⃣ Why did you use an aggregation pipeline in MongoDB instead of querying all documents?

To extract only unique IP values and reduce the amount of data processed in Python, improving performance and memory usage.

2️⃣ Why use IP2Location offline instead of an external API?

Offline lookup avoids API rate limits, reduces latency, and is more cost-effective for large-scale IP processing.

3️⃣ How do you handle invalid or missing IP addresses?

Invalid or empty IPs are filtered early, and IPs without location data are logged separately so they don’t affect the main pipeline.

4️⃣ How does this pipeline scale with large datasets?

It processes IPs in batches, logs progress periodically, and avoids repeated lookups by deduplicating IPs upfront.

5️⃣ Why do you write two separate output files?

Separating successful and failed records makes data quality issues explicit and allows retries or analysis without reprocessing valid data.

6️⃣ Why upload results to Google Cloud Storage?

GCS acts as a durable staging layer so the data can be ingested into BigQuery or reused by downstream pipelines.

7️⃣ What would you improve if this ran in production?

I would parallelize lookups, add retry/backoff logic, and convert the output to partitioned formats like Parquet for better downstream performance.

